lly parse the table's specific categorization rules to accurately calculate the total par amount for National Defense Series issues.\n\nThe key insight is focusing on the Callable column for each year, not the Fixed-maturity column. This means systematically reviewing each year's entries to identify callable securities, particularly those with National Defense Series designation. I'll methodically go through each section to ensure I capture all relevant callable amounts.\n\nFor 1941, no callable securities exist. In 1944, I notice the 3/4% Notes D has a specific callable range of 1944-1954, with a substantial callable amount of 1,037. However, the 1945 section shows a fixed-maturity note without callable features.\n\nI'll carefully track the National Defense Series securities, confirming their call dates and corresponding dollar amounts across different years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c274443832604dc4aa200aae","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json\nimport re\n\n# Load the JSON data\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1941_05.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Get the table from element 178\nelements = data['document']['elements']\ntable_html = elements[178]['content']\n\n# Simple HTML parsing - split by </tr>\nrows = table_html.split('</tr>')\n\n# Track the current year (first callable classification)\ncurrent_year = None\n\n# Find all National Defense Series items and classify by year first callable\nprint(\"Analyzing National Defense Series issues by year first callable:\")\nprint(\"=\"*70)\n\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>(.*?)</td>', row, re.DOTALL)\n    if cells:\n        cell_texts = [re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', cell).strip() for cell in cells]\n        first_col = cell_texts[0] if cell_texts else \"\"\n        \n        # Check if it's a year header (just a year like \"1941\")\n        if re.match(r'^\\d{4}$', first_col):\n            current_year = first_col\n            print(f\"\\n--- {current_year} (first callable year) ---\")\n        \n        # Check if it contains \"Nat. Defense Series\" or \"Defense Series\"\n        if 'Defense' in first_col:\n            fixed_col = cell_texts[1] if len(cell_texts) > 1 else \"\"\n            callable_col = cell_texts[2] if len(cell_texts) > 2 else \"\"\n            \n            print(f\"  Description: {first_col}\")\n            print(f\"    Fixed-maturity: {fixed_col}\")\n            print(f\"    Callable: {callable_col}\")\n            \n            # Determine year first callable from the description\n            # For example, \"9/15/44-54\" means first callable in 1944\n            # For bills, they don't have call features typically\n            if '44-54' in first_col:\n                print(f\"    -> First callable: 1944\")\n            elif '12/15/45' in first_col:\n                # This matures in 1945, but we need to check if it's callable\n                if callable_col and callable_col != '':\n                    print(f\"    -> First callable: 1945\")\n                else:\n                    print(f\"    -> Not callable (fixed maturity)\")\n            elif first_col.startswith('Bills'):\n                print(f\"    -> Bills (not callable in traditional sense)\")\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\nprint(\"\\nSummary - Total by year first callable:\")\nprint(\"1941: Bills (Nat. Defense Series) - 401 (but bills, not callable)\")\nprint(\"1944: 3/4% Notes D (Nat. Defense Series) - 9/15/44-54\")\nprint(\"      Callable amount: 1,037\")\nprint(\"1945: 3/4% Notes B (Nat. Defense Series) - 12/15/45\")\nprint(\"      Fixed amount: 531 (not callable)\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
