 is that the note \"3/4% Notes D (Nat. Defense Series) - 9/15/44-54\" has a specific maturity range, suggesting it's first callable in 1944. However, the classification seems inconsistent, as it's grouped under the 1943 header in the first callable section.\n\nThe total for 1943 shows 1,394 in fixed-maturity issues and 1,855 in callable issues, which provides context for how these securities are being categorized.\n\nI'm tracking the National Defense Series items, noting the complex mapping of callable years and security descriptions. The data reveals nuanced details about different series' call dates and maturity profiles, with each security having unique characteristics that don't follow a straightforward linear pattern.\n\nFor the Bills (Nat. Defense Series), they're listed as callable in 1941 but function more like bills with a fixed amount of 401. The 3/4% Notes D shows an interesting split between fixed and callable amounts, totaling 1,672, with 1944 as its first callable year. The 3/4% Notes B presents another variation, being fixed at 531 and not callable.\n\nThe total National Defense Series comes to 2,604, encompassing multiple series with distinct callable year characteristics.\n\nI'll break this down by first callable year, categorizing each security's callable status and amount. The 1941 bills are unique in their callability, while the 1944 and 1945 series have different callable features.\n\nThe total of 2,604 represents the combined callable amounts across different years, with 1944 contributing the majority at 1,672 and 1945 at 531.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_3066c103b94e441ba99761d5","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json\nimport re\n\n# Load the JSON data\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1941_05.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Get the table from element 178\nelements = data['document']['elements']\ntable_html = elements[178]['content']\n\n# Parse rows\nrows = table_html.split('</tr>')\n\ndef parse_value(val):\n    \"\"\"Parse value like '1,037' to integer 1037\"\"\"\n    if val == '-' or val == '' or val == 'nan':\n        return 0\n    try:\n        return int(val.replace(',', ''))\n    except:\n        return 0\n\n# Let me track by the actual year headers in the \"first callable\" classification\n# The table structure shows items by the year they are classified under\n# So items under \"1943\" header are those first callable in 1943\n\n# Collect National Defense Series items with their classified year\nnd_items = []\n\ncurrent_year = None\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>(.*?)</td>', row, re.DOTALL)\n    if cells and len(cells) >= 4:\n        cell_texts = [re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', cell).strip() for cell in cells[:4]]\n        first_col = cell_texts[0] if cell_texts else \"\"\n        \n        # Check if it's a year header\n        if re.match(r'^\\d{4}$', first_col):\n            current_year = first_col\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip totals\n        if 'Total' in first_col:\n            continue\n            \n        # Check for National Defense Series\n        if 'Defense' in first_col and 'Series' in first_col:\n            fixed_col = cell_texts[1] if len(cell_texts) > 1 else \"\"\n            callable_col = cell_texts[2] if len(cell_texts) > 2 else \"\"\n            \n            fixed_val = parse_value(fixed_col)\n            callable_val = parse_value(callable_col)\n            \n            nd_items.append({\n                'year_classified': current_year,\n                'description': first_col,\n                'fixed': fixed_val,\n                'callable': callable_val,\n                'total': fixed_val + callable_val\n            })\n\nprint(\"National Defense Series items by year classified (first callable classification):\")\nprint(\"=\"*80)\nfor item in nd_items:\n    print(f\"\\nYear {item['year_classified']}: {item['description']}\")\n    print(f\"  Fixed: {item['fixed']}, Callable: {item['callable']}, Total: {item['total']}\")\n\n# Now sum by year\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*80)\nprint(\"Total by year first callable:\")\ntotal_by_year = {}\nfor item in nd_items:\n    year = item['year_classified']\n    if year not in total_by_year:\n        total_by_year[year] = 0\n    total_by_year[year] += item['total']\n\nfor year in sorted(total_by_year.keys()):\n    print(f\"  {year}: {total_by_year[year]} million\")\n\ntotal_all = sum(total_by_year.values())\nprint(f\"\\nTOTAL: {total_all} million\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
