oking at row 26:\n- \"3/4% Notes D (Nat. Defense Series) - 9/15/44-54....\" has Fixed: 635, Callable: 1,037\n\nThis is a callable security. The format \"9/15/44-54\" typically means the issue matures in 1954 but is first callable in 1944.\n\nSo the actual first callable years are:\n1. Bills (Nat. Defense Series): Not really callable (due in 1941)\n2. 3/4% Notes D (Nat. Defense Series) - 9/15/44-54: First callable in 1944\n3. 3/4% Notes B (Nat. Defense Series) - 12/15/45: Fixed maturity (not callable)\n\nBut the question asks to use the maturity schedule as presented - \"classified by year in which they are first callable\" - which seems to mean the table's classification. The table groups securities by their first callable year, so I should follow that structure.\n\nMy interpretation of 2,604 appears correct. Looking at how the table organizes data: \"1941\" contains the Bills (Nat. Defense Series) at 401, while \"1943\" holds both the 3/4% Notes D (Nat. Defense Series) - 9/15/44-54 with 635 fixed and 1,037 callable (totaling 1,672) and the 3/4% Notes B (Nat. Defense Series) - 12/15/45 at 531.\n\nThis gives me 401 + 1672 + 531 = 2,604.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ded23955894b4a8abcac3248","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/app/answer.txt","content":"2604"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
