ntradictory. I need to check this more carefully - maybe it's actually listed under 1944?\n\nLooking at the data again:\n- Under \"1943\" header we have: Notes D (9/15/44-54) and Notes B (12/15/45)\n- Under \"1944\" header (which would come next) should be items first callable in 1944\n\nThe issue is that both the 1943 and 1944 headers appear to be grouped together in the table, which is unusual. I need to trace through the full table structure to see where exactly these securities are categorized.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_08ed62233512413f8f0d16d3","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json\nimport re\n\n# Load the JSON data\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1941_05.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nelements = data['document']['elements']\ntable_html = elements[178]['content']\n\n# Parse rows - look at all rows\nrows = table_html.split('</tr>')\n\n# Find years in column 1 and items under each\nprint(\"Looking for year headers:\")\ncurrent_year = None\nyear_positions = {}\n\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>(.*?)</td>', row, re.DOTALL)\n    if cells:\n        cell_texts = [re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', cell).strip() for cell in cells]\n        first_col = cell_texts[0] if cell_texts else \"\"\n        \n        # Check if it's a year header\n        if re.match(r'^\\d{4}$', first_col):\n            current_year = first_col\n            year_positions[current_year] = i\n            print(f\"Year {first_col} at row {i}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nYear header positions:\", year_positions)\n\n# Now find rows between each year header\n# 1941 ends at row 8 (Total)\n# 1942 ends at row 13 (Total)\n# 1943 should end around row 21 or 27?\n\n# The pattern shows that 1943 header is at row 14, then items including Notes D and Notes B appear\n# Then we see Total at row 21\n# Then at row 22-27 we see items again - but there's no 1944 header!\n\n# Wait -